flp-rulebook (0.0.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * verify_rulebase/1 and verify_activities/1: duplicate_priority now tells
    clauses apart by clause reference. Rules whose consequence is computed
    in the body (e.g. note(Text)) no longer report a false duplicate.
  * consider/1 prints the consequence text; it printed the literal term
    text(note(...)) before.
  * Tests for both.

 -- Andrew Dougherty <552578+aindilis@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:30:00 -0500

flp-rulebook (0.0.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Debian packaging: installs to /usr/share/flp-rulebook (engine, layers,
    load.pl, examples, vendored PyHOP); docs in /usr/share/doc/flp-rulebook.
  * LICENSE now holds the verbatim GPLv3 text (was a placeholder).
  * Makefile: check (same as test) and release targets.
  * README: installing the package and loading it from another program.

